{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>But Yehoshua bin Nun, etc., lived, etc.</b> There was no need to say this, since after the verse specified and said ״the men who brought an evil report of the land,״ you have thereby learned that none died except those who brought an evil report. Further, why was it necessary to say ״of the men״?" "<b>And it may be explained</b> according to what they said in tractate Bava Batra (Bava Batra 121b): It was taught: Yair ben Menasheh was born in the days of Yaakov, and they raised a difficulty from the fact that we find he entered the land, as it is written ״וַיַּכּוּ מֵהֶם אַנְשֵׁי הָעַי כִּשְׁלֹשִׁים וְשִׁשָּׁה אִישׁ״ (Joshua 7:5) etc. — this is Yair ben Menasheh, who was equal to the greatest member of the Sanhedrin. And Rav Acha answered that the decree was not pronounced upon anyone less than twenty years old nor upon anyone more than sixty. End quote. Now, from the fact that the Gemara did not answer that Yair was a perfect tzaddik, you see to know that the merit of a tzaddik did not save him from that decree. And this is the meaning of the verse's saying <b>but Yehoshua</b> etc. <b>lived</b> etc. — the reason they lived is that being among the men who went to spy is what stood for them; but had they not been among the spies and had remained within the general community of Israel, the decree would have come upon them as well, even though they were perfect tzaddikim, because they were above twenty and below sixty when they left Egypt." "<b>Further,</b> he alluded, in the manner of the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Ḥagigah 15a): one who is meritorious takes his portion and his fellow's portion in Gan Eden. So too Yehoshua and Calev increased their portion in life from the men who went to spy, for it is their right to take the spies' portion. They also said of blessed memory (Bava Batra 117b) that they took their portion in the land."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:39.279472581Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}